-- title:
--   Trichotomy for points of the integral model over a DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. the bundle of data and properties carried by the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` — the pushout of the spectra of the two chart algebras generated over $\mathbf Z$ by Igusa's $j$ and by $j^{-1}$ inside the full modular function field of level $p$ — together with its structure morphism `DRModel.toBase p` to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$; among the components of the package are the open subscheme $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{smoothLocus}$ of `DRModel p` and, for a field $\kappa$, the morphisms $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ into the base change of the model along $\mathbf Z \to \kappa$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is the ideal generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $\mathrm{to}\kappa \colon O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $x$ be a point of the fibre product of `DRModel.toBase p` with $\operatorname{Spec} O \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$. Then at least one of three alternatives holds: the second projection sends $x$ into the basic open set $D(p) \subseteq \operatorname{Spec} O$; the first projection sends $x$ into $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{smoothLocus}$; or there is a point $n$ of the fibre product of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ with $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ whose image under the first projection, followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ and then by the base-change morphism `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` from the $\kappa$-fibre product to the $O$-fibre product, equals $x$.
--
--   This is the covering trichotomy for the Deligne–Rapoport integral model base changed to a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$: a point lies over the generic point of $O$, or in the base change of the smooth locus, or is a crossing of the two components of the geometric fibre in characteristic $p$. It is the case division used for the local statements about that base change, being cited in the proofs of integral closedness and regularity of its stalks and in the construction of the resolved model.
